From d9dcd34228081d3ccb033370c9ab42683a1deceb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:15:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] add apex-sales: owner-only outbound engine that finds
 publishers and emails them

Brings back the automated sales engine removed with the TypeScript control
plane, as a std-only Rust crate (rust/crates/apex-sales). It is an internal
tool for getting customers for the console autopilot; customers never see it
and it is never sold.

Leads come from imported seed lists, apex-api free-audit requests and the
contacts in public app-ads.txt files. Discovery fetches app-ads.txt and App
Store data; every email cites one of those observations, and a contact with
no evidence is not emailed. An hourly run scores, ranks and sends; replies
and bounces are ingested and classified.

Models, each with documented priors:
- lead score: Bayesian logistic regression, Laplace updates (Chapelle & Li
  2011), probit-corrected predictions, exact log-odds reason codes
- value of a reply: Beta-Binomial funnel with empirical-Bayes pooling by size
  band; value-to-go credit for delayed outcomes
- ranking: expected value on a Thompson draw, net of send and complaint cost
- message choice: Thompson sampling on revenue value, top-two sampling
  (Russo 2016), discounting, complaint-safety exclusion
- timing and stopping: pooled Beta per local hour, per-step hazards
- domain health: Bayesian rate tests plus a Bernoulli cumulative-sum test,
  warm-up 20 to 150 per day, quarantine on breach
- measurement: randomized 10% holdout with a Newcombe interval; Brier, log
  loss, reliability bins, isotonic recalibration
- hygiene: Fellegi-Sunter linkage with Jaro-Winkler; RFC 3464/3834 reply
  rules plus naive Bayes; mediation platform inferred from DIRECT lines

Hard rules (suppression, country table, one active contact per publisher,
holdout, breaker, cap, grounding) sit in one decision gate. Shadow mode is
the default and only writes .eml previews.

The built-in simulator runs the production engine against a naive baseline
on the same synthetic market: 1.27x and 1.72x total value at 1200
publishers, 3.78x and 5.63x at 6000 publishers where ranking decides who
gets the capped sends.

Registered with CI: coverage matrix entry, floor 85 (measured 97.65 lines /
97.82 functions on rustc 1.97; margin for the 1.88 CI toolchain), policy
domain, suite, systemd unit contract. Hourly run and daily discover units,
deployment inventory entry and a runbook in docs/Internal/Sales.

